# Line endings are LF in the repository and LF in every working tree, Windows included.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout under `core.autocrlf=true` holds CRLF, and `rustfmt.toml` sets
# `newline_style = "Unix"` — so `cargo fmt --check`, and therefore `just ci`, fails on every source
# file before it reads a line of code. The shell scripts under `herdr/` and `scripts/` need LF to
# run at all, and Rust itself is indifferent.
#
# `text=auto` still leaves detected binary files alone, so the prebuilt syntax dumps are untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
